{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Nq6VwH19Lz3iagQjeKKNSv","type":"tool_result","content":"# GoReleaser v2 config for ard. Releases run from the release workflow on the\n# v* tags version.yml pushes; `make release-check` runs it locally as a snapshot.\nversion: 2\nproject_name: ard\n\nbuilds:\n  - id: ard\n    main: ./cmd/ard\n    binary: ard\n    env:\n      - CGO_ENABLED=0\n    goos: [darwin, linux]\n    goarch: [arm64, amd64]\n    flags:\n      - -trimpath\n    ldflags:\n      - -s -w -X main.version={{.Tag}}\n    mod_timestamp: \"{{ .CommitTimestamp }}\"\n\narchives:\n  - id: ard\n    formats: [tar.gz]\n    name_template: \"ard_{{ .Version }}_{{ .Os }}_{{ .Arch }}\"\n\nchecksum:\n  name_template: checksums.txt\n\n# version.yml already created the (notes-only) release; add files to it.\nrelease:\n  mode: keep-existing\n  github:\n    owner: albertcbrown\n    name: ard\n\nhomebrew_casks:\n  - name: ard\n    directory: Casks\n    homepage: https://github.com/albertcbrown/ard\n    description: Autonomous repository development agents driven by GitHub issues\n    # The token comes from the environment of the release workflow.\n    repository:\n      owner: albertcbrown\n      name: homebrew-tap\n      token: \"{{ .Env.TAP_GITHUB_TOKEN }}\"\n    url:\n      template: \"https://github.com/albertcbrown/ard/releases/download/{{ .Tag }}/{{ .ArtifactName }}\"\n    dependencies:\n      - formula: git\n    caveats: |\n      ard runs agents that need the claude CLI and either CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN\n      or an API key in the environment.\n    # Accepted risk (see docs/proposal.md): the binary is not signed or notarized\n    # yet, so Gatekeeper's quarantine flag is cleared after install.\n    hooks:\n      post:\n        install: |\n          system_command \"/usr/bin/xattr\",\n                         args: [\"-dr\", \"com.apple.quarantine\", \"#{staged_path}/ard\"]\n# Release: build ard with GoReleaser and attach the archives and checksums to\n# the notes-only release version.yml created for a v* tag, then update the\n# Homebrew cask in albertcbrown/homebrew-tap.\n#\n# Inert until switched on: it does nothing unless the repository variable\n# ARD_VERSIONING is \"on\" and the release environment holds TAP_GITHUB_TOKEN\n# (a token that can push to albertcbrown/homebrew-tap only). Without the token\n# it says so and stops; it never half-publishes.\n#\n# Only the newest v* tag is released on a tag push, so version.yml's backfill\n# of many historical tags does not publish one release per tag. Use\n# workflow_dispatch with a tag to build an older one on purpose.\n#\n# Settings and recovery: docs/runbooks/release.md. Design: docs/proposal.md\n# (Delivery) and #177.\nname: release\n\non:\n  push:\n    tags: ['v*']\n  workflow_dispatch:\n    inputs:\n      tag:\n        description: Tag to release (vX.Y.Z); must already have a release\n        required: true\n        type: string\n\n# One release at a time; never cancel one that is uploading.\nconcurrency:\n  group: release\n  cancel-in-progress: false\n\npermissions:\n  contents: read\n\njobs:\n  release:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    timeout-minutes: 30\n    environment: release\n    permissions:\n      contents: write # upload assets to the existing release only\n    env:\n      ENABLED: ${{ vars.ARD_VERSIONING }}\n      EVENT: ${{ github.event_name }}\n      PUSHED_TAG: ${{ github.ref_name }}\n      INPUT_TAG: ${{ inputs.tag }}\n      HAS_TAP_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.TAP_GITHUB_TOKEN != '' }}\n    steps:\n      - name: Decide\n        id: decide\n        shell: bash\n        run: |\n          set -euo pipefail\n          skip() { echo \"::notice title=release::$1\"; echo \"run=false\" >>\"$GITHUB_OUTPUT\"; exit 0; }\n          [[ \"${ENABLED:-}\" == on ]] || skip \"ARD_VERSIONING is not on; nothing to release\"\n          [[ \"${HAS_TAP_TOKEN:-}\" == true ]] || skip \"the release environment has no TAP_GITHUB_TOKEN; create the tap token first (docs/runbooks/release.md)\"\n          if [[ \"$EVENT\" == workflow_dispatch ]]; then tag=$INPUT_TAG; else tag=$PUSHED_TAG; fi\n          [[ \"$tag\" =~ ^v(0|[1-9][0-9]*)\\.(0|[1-9][0-9]*)\\.(0|[1-9][0-9]*)$ ]] || { echo \"::error title=release::not a vX.Y.Z tag: $tag\"; exit 2; }\n          echo \"tag=$tag\" >>\"$GITHUB_OUTPUT\"\n          echo \"run=true\" >>\"$GITHUB_OUTPUT\"\n\n      - uses: actions/checkout@11d5960a326750d5838078e36cf38b85af677262 # v4.4.0\n        if: steps.decide.outputs.run == 'true'\n        with:\n          ref: refs/tags/${{ steps.decide.outputs.tag }}\n          fetch-depth: 0\n          fetch-tags: true\n          persist-credentials: false\n\n      - name: Newest tag only on push\n        id: newest\n        if: steps.decide.outputs.run == 'true'\n        shell: bash\n        env:\n          TAG: ${{ steps.decide.outputs.tag }}\n        run: |\n          set -euo pipefail\n          newest=$(git tag -l 'v*' | grep -E '^v(0|[1-9][0-9]*)\\.(0|[1-9][0-9]*)\\.(0|[1-9][0-9]*)$' | sort -V | tail -n 1)\n          if [[ \"$EVENT\" == push && \"$TAG\" != \"$newest\" ]]; then\n.github/workflows/release.yml:10:# Only the newest v* tag is released on a tag push, so version.yml's backfill\n.github/workflows/release.yml:72:        id: newest\n.github/workflows/release.yml:79:          newest=$(git tag -l 'v*' | grep -E '^v(0|[1-9][0-9]*)\\.(0|[1-9][0-9]*)\\.(0|[1-9][0-9]*)$' | sort -V | tail -n 1)\n.github/workflows/release.yml:80:          if [[ \"$EVENT\" == push && \"$TAG\" != \"$newest\" ]]; then\n.github/workflows/release.yml:81:            echo \"::notice title=release::$TAG is not the newest tag ($newest); skipping (dispatch with tag=$TAG to build it)\"\n.github/workflows/release.yml:88:        if: steps.newest.outputs.run == 'true'\n.github/workflows/release.yml:96:            || { echo \"::error title=release::no release for $TAG; version.yml creates it first\"; exit 2; }\n.github/workflows/release.yml:99:        if: steps.newest.outputs.run == 'true'\n.github/workflows/release.yml:105:        if: steps.newest.outputs.run == 'true'\n.github/workflows/version.yml:2:# tags every untagged first-parent commit after the newest version tag, oldest\n552:- **Gatekeeper: unsigned binary, quarantine cleared (accepted risk).** The release binary is neither signed nor notarized. The Homebrew cask removes `com.apple.quarantine` from the installed binary in `hooks.post.install`, which skips Gatekeeper's check, so the install path trusts the release archive, its checksum and whoever holds `TAP_GITHUB_TOKEN`. The owner accepts this. The follow-up is Developer ID signing and notarization in the release workflow, after which the hook is removed.\n593:- **Homebrew ([#177](https://github.com/albertcbrown/ard/issues/177)).** `.github/workflows/release.yml` builds each new `v*` tag with GoReleaser (`.goreleaser.yaml`: darwin and linux, arm64 and amd64, CGO off, `-X main.version`), adds the archives and `checksums.txt` to the release `version.yml` created (`release.mode: keep-existing`) and updates the cask in `albertcbrown/homebrew-tap` with `TAP_GITHUB_TOKEN`, a token scoped to the tap and held only in the `release` environment. It stays inert until `ARD_VERSIONING` is `on` and that token exists, and on a tag push it releases only the newest tag, so a backfill publishes once. Gatekeeper: the binary is not yet signed or notarized, so the cask clears the quarantine flag after install (`hooks.post.install`), an accepted risk; notarization is a follow-up.\n607:    P4 --> P5[\"Phase 5: Distribution<br/>versioned releases<br/>Homebrew cask\"]\n610:Phases 4 and 5 have no gate: Phase 4 ([#178](https://github.com/albertcbrown/ard/issues/178)) writes the user documentation and publishes it as a GitHub Pages site, and Phase 5 ([#177](https://github.com/albertcbrown/ard/issues/177)) publishes versioned releases and a Homebrew cask (`brew install --cask albertcbrown/tap/ard`). It ships the README Install section and the release runbook (`docs/runbooks/release.md`).\n000000b0: 6269 6e2f 6172 6460 206f 6e20 796f 7572  bin/ard` on your\n000000c0: 2060 5041 5448 602e                       `PATH`.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e4e61b66-dc6c-4556-82d6-966b5d078428","uuid":"7bacd48c-270f-4e7e-a704-4f70abf0dd33","timestamp":"2026-11-26T19:14:32.635Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# GoReleaser v2 config for ard. Releases run from the release workflow on the\n# v* tags version.yml pushes; `make release-check` runs it locally as a snapshot.\nversion: 2\nproject_name: ard\n\nbuilds:\n  - id: ard\n    main: ./cmd/ard\n    binary: ard\n    env:\n      - CGO_ENABLED=0\n    goos: [darwin, linux]\n    goarch: [arm64, amd64]\n    flags:\n      - -trimpath\n    ldflags:\n      - -s -w -X main.version={{.Tag}}\n    mod_timestamp: \"{{ .CommitTimestamp }}\"\n\narchives:\n  - id: ard\n    formats: [tar.gz]\n    name_template: \"ard_{{ .Version }}_{{ .Os }}_{{ .Arch }}\"\n\nchecksum:\n  name_template: checksums.txt\n\n# version.yml already created the (notes-only) release; add files to it.\nrelease:\n  mode: keep-existing\n  github:\n    owner: albertcbrown\n    name: ard\n\nhomebrew_casks:\n  - name: ard\n    directory: Casks\n    homepage: https://github.com/albertcbrown/ard\n    description: Autonomous repository development agents driven by GitHub issues\n    # The token comes from the environment of the release workflow.\n    repository:\n      owner: albertcbrown\n      name: homebrew-tap\n      token: \"{{ .Env.TAP_GITHUB_TOKEN }}\"\n    url:\n      template: \"https://github.com/albertcbrown/ard/releases/download/{{ .Tag }}/{{ .ArtifactName }}\"\n    dependencies:\n      - formula: git\n    caveats: |\n      ard runs agents that need the claude CLI and either CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN\n      or an API key in the environment.\n    # Accepted risk (see docs/proposal.md): the binary is not signed or notarized\n    # yet, so Gatekeeper's quarantine flag is cleared after install.\n    hooks:\n      post:\n        install: |\n          system_command \"/usr/bin/xattr\",\n                         args: [\"-dr\", \"com.apple.quarantine\", \"#{staged_path}/ard\"]\n# Release: build ard with GoReleaser and attach the archives and checksums to\n# the notes-only release version.yml created for a v* tag, then update the\n# Homebrew cask in albertcbrown/homebrew-tap.\n#\n# Inert until switched on: it does nothing unless the repository variable\n# ARD_VERSIONING is \"on\" and the release environment holds TAP_GITHUB_TOKEN\n# (a token that can push to albertcbrown/homebrew-tap only). Without the token\n# it says so and stops; it never half-publishes.\n#\n# Only the newest v* tag is released on a tag push, so version.yml's backfill\n# of many historical tags does not publish one release per tag. Use\n# workflow_dispatch with a tag to build an older one on purpose.\n#\n# Settings and recovery: docs/runbooks/release.md. Design: docs/proposal.md\n# (Delivery) and #177.\nname: release\n\non:\n  push:\n    tags: ['v*']\n  workflow_dispatch:\n    inputs:\n      tag:\n        description: Tag to release (vX.Y.Z); must already have a release\n        required: true\n        type: string\n\n# One release at a time; never cancel one that is uploading.\nconcurrency:\n  group: release\n  cancel-in-progress: false\n\npermissions:\n  contents: read\n\njobs:\n  release:\n    runs-on: ubuntu-latest\n    timeout-minutes: 30\n    environment: release\n    permissions:\n      contents: write # upload assets to the existing release only\n    env:\n      ENABLED: ${{ vars.ARD_VERSIONING }}\n      EVENT: ${{ github.event_name }}\n      PUSHED_TAG: ${{ github.ref_name }}\n      INPUT_TAG: ${{ inputs.tag }}\n      HAS_TAP_TOKEN: ${{ secrets.TAP_GITHUB_TOKEN != '' }}\n    steps:\n      - name: Decide\n        id: decide\n        shell: bash\n        run: |\n          set -euo pipefail\n          skip() { echo \"::notice title=release::$1\"; echo \"run=false\" >>\"$GITHUB_OUTPUT\"; exit 0; }\n          [[ \"${ENABLED:-}\" == on ]] || skip \"ARD_VERSIONING is not on; nothing to release\"\n          [[ \"${HAS_TAP_TOKEN:-}\" == true ]] || skip \"the release environment has no TAP_GITHUB_TOKEN; create the tap token first (docs/runbooks/release.md)\"\n          if [[ \"$EVENT\" == workflow_dispatch ]]; then tag=$INPUT_TAG; else tag=$PUSHED_TAG; fi\n          [[ \"$tag\" =~ ^v(0|[1-9][0-9]*)\\.(0|[1-9][0-9]*)\\.(0|[1-9][0-9]*)$ ]] || { echo \"::error title=release::not a vX.Y.Z tag: $tag\"; exit 2; }\n          echo \"tag=$tag\" >>\"$GITHUB_OUTPUT\"\n          echo \"run=true\" >>\"$GITHUB_OUTPUT\"\n\n      - uses: actions/checkout@11d5960a326750d5838078e36cf38b85af677262 # v4.4.0\n        if: steps.decide.outputs.run == 'true'\n        with:\n          ref: refs/tags/${{ steps.decide.outputs.tag }}\n          fetch-depth: 0\n          fetch-tags: true\n          persist-credentials: false\n\n      - name: Newest tag only on push\n        id: newest\n        if: steps.decide.outputs.run == 'true'\n        shell: bash\n        env:\n          TAG: ${{ steps.decide.outputs.tag }}\n        run: |\n          set -euo pipefail\n          newest=$(git tag -l 'v*' | grep -E '^v(0|[1-9][0-9]*)\\.(0|[1-9][0-9]*)\\.(0|[1-9][0-9]*)$' | sort -V | tail -n 1)\n          if [[ \"$EVENT\" == push && \"$TAG\" != \"$newest\" ]]; then\n.github/workflows/release.yml:10:# Only the newest v* tag is released on a tag push, so version.yml's backfill\n.github/workflows/release.yml:72:        id: newest\n.github/workflows/release.yml:79:          newest=$(git tag -l 'v*' | grep -E '^v(0|[1-9][0-9]*)\\.(0|[1-9][0-9]*)\\.(0|[1-9][0-9]*)$' | sort -V | tail -n 1)\n.github/workflows/release.yml:80:          if [[ \"$EVENT\" == push && \"$TAG\" != \"$newest\" ]]; then\n.github/workflows/release.yml:81:            echo \"::notice title=release::$TAG is not the newest tag ($newest); skipping (dispatch with tag=$TAG to build it)\"\n.github/workflows/release.yml:88:        if: steps.newest.outputs.run == 'true'\n.github/workflows/release.yml:96:            || { echo \"::error title=release::no release for $TAG; version.yml creates it first\"; exit 2; }\n.github/workflows/release.yml:99:        if: steps.newest.outputs.run == 'true'\n.github/workflows/release.yml:105:        if: steps.newest.outputs.run == 'true'\n.github/workflows/version.yml:2:# tags every untagged first-parent commit after the newest version tag, oldest\n552:- **Gatekeeper: unsigned binary, quarantine cleared (accepted risk).** The release binary is neither signed nor notarized. The Homebrew cask removes `com.apple.quarantine` from the installed binary in `hooks.post.install`, which skips Gatekeeper's check, so the install path trusts the release archive, its checksum and whoever holds `TAP_GITHUB_TOKEN`. The owner accepts this. The follow-up is Developer ID signing and notarization in the release workflow, after which the hook is removed.\n593:- **Homebrew ([#177](https://github.com/albertcbrown/ard/issues/177)).** `.github/workflows/release.yml` builds each new `v*` tag with GoReleaser (`.goreleaser.yaml`: darwin and linux, arm64 and amd64, CGO off, `-X main.version`), adds the archives and `checksums.txt` to the release `version.yml` created (`release.mode: keep-existing`) and updates the cask in `albertcbrown/homebrew-tap` with `TAP_GITHUB_TOKEN`, a token scoped to the tap and held only in the `release` environment. It stays inert until `ARD_VERSIONING` is `on` and that token exists, and on a tag push it releases only the newest tag, so a backfill publishes once. Gatekeeper: the binary is not yet signed or notarized, so the cask clears the quarantine flag after install (`hooks.post.install`), an accepted risk; notarization is a follow-up.\n607:    P4 --> P5[\"Phase 5: Distribution<br/>versioned releases<br/>Homebrew cask\"]\n610:Phases 4 and 5 have no gate: Phase 4 ([#178](https://github.com/albertcbrown/ard/issues/178)) writes the user documentation and publishes it as a GitHub Pages site, and Phase 5 ([#177](https://github.com/albertcbrown/ard/issues/177)) publishes versioned releases and a Homebrew cask (`brew install --cask albertcbrown/tap/ard`). It ships the README Install section and the release runbook (`docs/runbooks/release.md`).\n000000b0: 6269 6e2f 6172 6460 206f 6e20 796f 7572  bin/ard` on your\n000000c0: 2060 5041 5448 602e                       `PATH`.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Nq6VwH19Lz3iagQjeKKNSv","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
